./analysis/current_full_deepseek_replicate_agreement/include_unstable_cases_with_agent_outputs.csv:10:                  CLOP-DiT is a computational pipeline that generates synthetic single-cell gene expression profiles from structured biological descriptions (cell type, tissue, organism, marker genes, and disease context). It first learns to align text descriptions with real cell data in a shared mathematical space, then uses a diffusion model to generate new cell states matching a given description. The generated cells capture correct cell-type identity and marker gene patterns, but do not yet reproduce the full cell-to-cell variability seen in real single-cell experiments. This work demonstrates that text-guided single-cell generation is feasible as a proof of concept, opening directions for future simulation and hypothesis-generation tools in biology.",2026.0,"{""paper_type"": ""primary_model_paper"", ""bio_modality_present"": ""yes"", ""text_component_present"": ""unclear"", ""text_bio_bridge_present"": ""unclear"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""none"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""text_component_unclear"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""BiomedBERT text embeddings used for structured metadata fields"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""text–cell alignment via contrastive learning and conditional generation on text embeddings"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""not_assessed"", ""boundary_case"": ""text_component_boundary"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The paper presents a new model (CLOP-DiT) for single-cell generation conditioned on structured metadata fields (cell type, tissue, etc.) using BiomedBERT text embeddings. However, the text component is structured categorical metadata, not free natural language, making it unclear whether it meets the text component criterion.""}",primary_model_paper,yes,unclear,unclear,none,text_component_unclear,BiomedBERT text embeddings used for structured metadata fields,text–cell alignment via contrastive learning and conditional generation on text embeddings,not_assessed,text_component_boundary,"The paper presents a new model (CLOP-DiT) for single-cell generation conditioned on structured metadata fields (cell type, tissue, etc.) using BiomedBERT text embeddings. However, the text component is structured categorical metadata, not free natural language, making it unclear whether it meets the text component criterion.","{""paper_type"": ""primary_model_paper"", ""generative_model_present"": ""yes"", ""foundation_model_evidence"": ""unclear"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""none"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""conditional Diffusion Transformer (DiT) generates scGPT-compatible latent states via flow matching"", ""boundary_case"": ""clear_include"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract describes a conditional Diffusion Transformer that generates single-cell transcriptomic profiles from structured biological descriptions, clearly a generative model with text-to-bio generation.""}",primary_model_paper,yes,unclear,none,none,not_assessed,not_assessed,conditional Diffusion Transformer (DiT) generates scGPT-compatible latent states via flow matching,clear_include,"The abstract describes a conditional Diffusion Transformer that generates single-cell transcriptomic profiles from structured biological descriptions, clearly a generative model with text-to-bio generation.",UNCERTAIN,PASS,True,"{""paper_type"": ""primary_model_paper"", ""bio_modality_present"": ""yes"", ""text_component_present"": ""yes"", ""text_bio_bridge_present"": ""yes"", ""generative_model_present"": ""yes"", ""foundation_model_evidence"": ""yes"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""none"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""BiomedBERT text embeddings; structured biological descriptions"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""contrastive aligner maps BiomedBERT text embeddings and scGPT cell embeddings into a shared space; conditional generation steered by biological template"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""conditional Diffusion Transformer generates scGPT-compatible latent states via flow matching"", ""boundary_case"": ""clear_include"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract presents CLOP-DiT, a new model that generates single-cell profiles conditioned on structured text descriptions via contrastive alignment and diffusion transformer, satisfying all inclusion criteria.""}",primary_model_paper,yes,yes,yes,yes,yes,none,none,BiomedBERT text embeddings; structured biological descriptions,contrastive aligner maps BiomedBERT text embeddings and scGPT cell embeddings into a shared space; conditional generation steered by biological template,conditional Diffusion Transformer generates scGPT-compatible latent states via flow matching,clear_include,"The abstract presents CLOP-DiT, a new model that generates single-cell profiles conditioned on structured text descriptions via contrastive alignment and diffusion transformer, satisfying all inclusion criteria.",UNCERTAIN|PASS,primary_model_paper,yes,yes,yes,yes,yes,,,BiomedBERT text embeddings; structured biological descriptions,contrastive aligner maps BiomedBERT text embeddings and scGPT cell embeddings into a shared space; conditional generation steered by biological template,conditional Diffusion Transformer generates scGPT-compatible latent states via flow matching,clear_include,"The abstract presents CLOP-DiT, a new model that generates single-cell profiles conditioned on structured text descriptions via contrastive alignment and diffusion transformer, satisfying all inclusion criteria.",INCLUDE,,,INCLUDE,,,False,CLOP-DiT: Structured-Metadata-Conditioned Single-Cell Latent Generation via Contrastive Language-Omics Pretraining and Diffusion Transformers,10.64898/2026.03.26.714457,"Abstract
./analysis/current_full_deepseek_replicate_agreement/include_unstable_cases_with_agent_outputs.csv:18:                  CLOP-DiT is a computational pipeline that generates synthetic single-cell gene expression profiles from structured biological descriptions (cell type, tissue, organism, marker genes, and disease context). It first learns to align text descriptions with real cell data in a shared mathematical space, then uses a diffusion model to generate new cell states matching a given description. The generated cells capture correct cell-type identity and marker gene patterns, but do not yet reproduce the full cell-to-cell variability seen in real single-cell experiments. This work demonstrates that text-guided single-cell generation is feasible as a proof of concept, opening directions for future simulation and hypothesis-generation tools in biology.",2026.0,"{""paper_type"": ""primary_model_paper"", ""bio_modality_present"": ""yes"", ""text_component_present"": ""unclear"", ""text_bio_bridge_present"": ""unclear"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""none"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""mixed_signals"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""BiomedBERT text embeddings; five-field biological template (cell type, tissue, organism, marker genes, disease)"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""text–cell alignment; contrastive language-omics pretraining; generation conditioned on structured metadata"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""not_assessed"", ""boundary_case"": ""thin_abstract_boundary"", ""decision_rationale"": ""Presents a new generative model for single-cell data conditioned on structured metadata using text embeddings, but it is unclear whether the conditioning inputs constitute natural-language text or structured labels, making text component and bridge uncertain.""}",primary_model_paper,yes,unclear,unclear,none,mixed_signals,"BiomedBERT text embeddings; five-field biological template (cell type, tissue, organism, marker genes, disease)",text–cell alignment; con