 aligner maps text and cell embeddings into shared space; conditional generation on metadata fields"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""conditional Diffusion Transformer generates latents via flow matching; generates synthetic single-cell gene expression profiles"", ""boundary_case"": ""thin_abstract_boundary"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract presents a primary model paper with a generative diffusion model for single-cell data conditioned on structured metadata fields, but it is unclear whether the metadata fields constitute natural-language text as required for text component and text-bio bridge; thus text_component_present and text_bio_bridge_present remain unclear.""}",primary_model_paper,yes,unclear,unclear,yes,no,none,mixed_signals,BiomedBERT text embeddings; five-field biological template,contrastive aligner maps text and cell embeddings into shared space; conditional generation on metadata fields,conditional Diffusion Transformer generates latents via flow matching; generates synthetic single-cell gene expression profiles,thin_abstract_boundary,"The abstract presents a primary model paper with a generative diffusion model for single-cell data conditioned on structured metadata fields, but it is unclear whether the metadata fields constitute natural-language text as required for text component and text-bio bridge; thus text_component_present and text_bio_bridge_present remain unclear.",UNCERTAIN|PASS,primary_model_paper,yes,unclear,unclear,yes,no,,mixed_signals,BiomedBERT text embeddings; five-field biological template,contrastive aligner maps text and cell embeddings into shared space; conditional generation on metadata fields,conditional Diffusion Transformer generates latents via flow matching; generates synthetic single-cell gene expression profiles,thin_abstract_boundary,"The abstract presents a primary model paper with a generative diffusion model for single-cell data conditioned on structured metadata fields, but it is unclear whether the metadata fields constitute natural-language text as required for text component and text-bio bridge; thus text_component_present and text_bio_bridge_present remain unclear.",UNCERTAIN,,text_component_unclear,UNCERTAIN,,text_component_unclear,True
./analysis/current_full_deepseek_replicate_agreement/include_unstable_cases_with_agent_outputs.csv:19:982,ClinClip: a Multimodal Language Pre-training model integrating EEG data for enhanced English medical listening assessment,10.3389/fnins.2024.1493163,"Introduction In the field of medical listening assessments,accurate transcription and effective cognitive load management are critical for enhancing healthcare delivery. Traditional speech recognition systems, while successful in general applications often struggle in medical contexts where the cognitive state of the listener plays a significant role. These conventional methods typically rely on audio–only inputs and lack the ability to account for the listener's cognitive load, leading to reduced accuracy and effectiveness in complex medical environments. Methods To address these limitations, this study introduces ClinClip, a novel multimodal model that integrates EEG signals with audio data through a transformer-based architecture. ClinClip is designed to dynamically adjust to the cognitive state of the listener, thereby improving transcription accuracy and robustness in medical settings. The model leverages cognitive-enhanced strategies, including EEG-based modulation and hierarchical fusion of multimodal data, to overcome the challenges faced by traditional methods. Results and discussion Experiments conducted on four datasets–EEGEyeNet, DEAP, PhyAAt, and eSports Sensors–demonstrate that ClinClip significantly outperforms six state-of-the-art models in both Word Error Rate (WER) and Cognitive Modulation Efficiency (CME). These results underscore the model's effectiveness in handling complex medical audio scenarios and highlight its potential to improve the accuracy of medical listening assessments. By addressing the cognitive aspects of the listening process. ClinClip contributes to more reliable and effective healthcare delivery, offering a substantial advancement over traditional speech recognition approaches.",2024.0,"{""paper_type"": ""primary_model_paper"", ""bio_modality_present"": ""no"", ""text_component_present"": ""yes"", ""text_bio_bridge_present"": ""no"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""EC1_no_bio_modality"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""transcription accuracy, Word Error Rate"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""not_assessed"", ""boundary_case"": ""clear_exclude"", ""decision_rationale"": ""ClinClip integrates EEG and audio for speech transcription; no biological data modality (e.g., omics, cells, molecules) is central. Therefore excluded under EC1_no_bio_modality.""}",primary_model_paper,no,yes,no,EC1_no_bio_modality,none,"transcription accuracy, Word Error Rate",none,not_assessed,clear_exclude,"ClinClip integrates EEG and audio for speech transcription; no biological data modality (e.g., omics, cells, molecules) is central. Therefore excluded under EC1_no_bio_modality.","{""paper_type"": ""primary_model_paper"", ""generative_model_present"": ""unclear"", ""foundation_model_evidence"": ""unclear"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""none"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""generative_status_unclear"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""none"", ""boundary_case"": ""generative_boundary"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract describes a multimodal transformer for medical transcription but does not explicitly state a generative mechanism (e.g., decoder, autoregressive, seq2seq). Generative status is unclear; foundation model evidence is lacking.""}",primary_model_paper,unclear,unclear,none,generative_status_unclear,not_assessed,not_assessed,none,generative_boundary,"The abstract describes a multimodal transformer for medical transcription but does not explicitly state a generative mechanism (e.g., decoder, autoregressive, seq2seq). Generative status is unclear; foundation model evide