./analysis/current_full_deepseek_replicate_agreement/include_unstable_cases_with_agent_outputs.csv:29:3214,Geneverse: A collection of Open-source Multimodal Large Language Models for Genomic and Proteomic Research,,"The applications of large language models (LLMs) are promising for biomedical and healthcare research. Despite the availability of open-source LLMs trained using a wide range of biomedical data, current research on the applications of LLMs to genomics and proteomics is still limited. To fill this gap, we propose a collection of finetuned LLMs and multimodal LLMs (MLLMs), known as Geneverse, for three novel tasks in genomic and proteomic research. The models in Geneverse are trained and evaluated based on domain-specific datasets, and we use advanced parameter-efficient finetuning techniques to achieve the model adaptation for tasks including the generation of descriptions for gene functions, protein function inference from its structure, and marker gene selection from spatial transcriptomic data. We demonstrate that adapted LLMs and MLLMs perform well for these tasks and may outperform closed-source large-scale models based on our evaluations focusing on both truthfulness and structural correctness. All of the training strategies and base models we used are freely accessible.",2024.0,"{""paper_type"": ""primary_model_paper"", ""bio_modality_present"": ""yes"", ""text_component_present"": ""yes"", ""text_bio_bridge_present"": ""yes"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""none"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""generation of descriptions for gene functions"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""generation of descriptions for gene functions"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""not_assessed"", ""boundary_case"": ""clear_include"", ""decision_rationale"": ""Presents Geneverse, a collection of finetuned LLMs/MLLMs for genomic and proteomic tasks including generating gene function descriptions, satisfying text and bio bridge.""}",primary_model_paper,yes,yes,yes,none,none,generation of descriptions for gene functions,generation of descriptions for gene functions,not_assessed,clear_include,"Presents Geneverse, a collection of finetuned LLMs/MLLMs for genomic and proteomic tasks including generating gene function descriptions, satisfying text and bio bridge.","{""paper_type"": ""application_wrapper"", ""generative_model_present"": ""yes"", ""foundation_model_evidence"": ""no"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""application_wrapper"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""generation of descriptions for gene functions"", ""boundary_case"": ""wrapper_boundary"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The paper finetunes existing LLMs for domain-specific tasks including generating gene function descriptions, but does not introduce a new foundation model; it is an application wrapper.""}",application_wrapper,yes,no,application_wrapper,none,not_assessed,not_assessed,generation of descriptions for gene functions,wrapper_boundary,"The paper finetunes existing LLMs for domain-specific tasks including generating gene function descriptions, but does not introduce a new foundation model; it is an application wrapper.",PASS,EXCLUDE,True,"{""paper_type"": ""application_wrapper"", ""bio_modality_present"": ""yes"", ""text_component_present"": ""yes"", ""text_bio_bridge_present"": ""yes"", ""generative_model_present"": ""yes"", ""foundation_model_evidence"": ""no"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""application_wrapper"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""generation of descriptions for gene functions"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""generation of descriptions for gene functions from biological data"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""generation of descriptions for gene functions"", ""boundary_case"": ""wrapper_boundary"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract presents finetuned LLMs and MLLMs for specific tasks, not a new foundational model, so it is an application wrapper. The description generation task provides clear evidence for text component and text-bio bridge.""}",application_wrapper,yes,yes,yes,yes,no,application_wrapper,none,generation of descriptions for gene functions,generation of descriptions for gene functions from biological data,generation of descriptions for gene functions,wrapper_boundary,"The abstract presents finetuned LLMs and MLLMs for specific tasks, not a new foundational model, so it is an application wrapper. The description generation task provides clear evidence for text component and text-bio bridge.",PASS|EXCLUDE,application_wrapper,yes,yes,yes,yes,no,application_wrapper,,generation of descriptions for gene functions,generation of descriptions for gene functions from biological data,generation of descriptions for gene functions,wrapper_boundary,"The abstract presents finetuned LLMs and MLLMs for specific tasks, not a new foundational model, so it is an application wrapper. The description generation task provides clear evidence for text component and text-bio bridge.",EXCLUDE,application_wrapper,,EXCLUDE,application_wrapper,,False,Geneverse: A collection of Open-source Multimodal Large Language Models for Genomic and Proteomic Research,,"The applications of large language models (LLMs) are promising for biomedical and healthcare research. Despite the availability of open-source LLMs trained using a wide range of biomedical data, current research on the applications of LLMs to genomics and proteomics is still limited. To fill this gap, we propose a collection of finetuned LLMs and multimodal LLMs (MLLMs), known as Geneverse, for three novel tasks in genomic and proteomic research. The models in Geneverse are trained and evaluated based on domain-specific datasets, and we use advanced parameter-efficient finetuning techniques to achieve the model adaptation for tasks including the generation of descriptions for gene functions, protein function inference from its structure, and marker gene selection from spatial transcriptomic data. We demonstrate that adapted LLMs and MLLMs perform well for these tasks and may outperform closed-source large-scale models based on our evaluations focusing on both truthfulness and structural correctness. All of the training strategies and base models we used are freely accessible.",2024.0,"{""paper_type"": ""primary_model_paper"", ""bio_modality_present"": ""yes"", ""text_component_present"": ""yes"", ""text_bio_bridge_present"": ""yes"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""none"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""generation of descriptions for gene functions"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": ""generation of descriptions for gene functions, protein function inference from its structure"", ""evidence_for_generative_model"": ""not_assessed"", ""boundary_case"": ""clear_include"", ""decision_rationale"": ""The abstract presents a new collection of finetuned LLMs and MLLMs (Geneverse) for genomic and proteomic tasks that include generating natural-language descriptions from biological data, clearly satisfying text component and text-bio bridge criteria.""}",primary_model_paper,yes,yes,yes,none,none,generation of descriptions for gene functions,"generation of descriptions for gene functions, protein function inference from its structure",not_assessed,clear_include,"The abstract presents a new collection of finetuned LLMs and MLLMs (Geneverse) for genomic and proteomic tasks that include generating natural-language descriptions from biological data, clearly satisfying text component and text-bio bridge criteria.","{""paper_type"": ""primary_model_paper"", ""generative_model_present"": ""yes"", ""foundation_model_evidence"": ""no"", ""primary_exclusion_code"": ""none"", ""uncertainty_reason"": ""none"", ""evidence_for_text_component"": ""not_assessed"", ""evidence_for_text_bio_bridge"": 