./analysis/cross_agent_screening_agreement_current_3ds_2gpt/cross_model_decisions.csv:121: This study demonstrates that multi-modal MRIs can successfully identify glioblastoma subtypes characterized by deep learning derived radiomic features. Future work will focus on validation with comprehensive molecular and tissue-based profiles, survival outcomes, and treatment responses to support personalized medicine.",exclude_uncertain_unstable,EXCLUDE,application_wrapper,,application_wrapper,no,no,no,yes,none,none,"Masked Auto-Encoder (MAE), a deep learning architecture trained through self-supervised learning",clear_exclude,"The abstract describes a deep learning-based radiomic subtyping study using MAE for feature extraction and clustering, with no natural-language text component, no text-bio bridge, and no generative mechanism; it is an application wrapper and not eligible.",This paper uses a Masked Auto-Encoder on MRI data for subtyping glioblastoma; no natural-language text component or text-bio bridge is described.,"The paper uses a Masked Auto-Encoder for MRI feature extraction and clustering to identify glioblastoma subtypes, with no mention of generative text or biological sequence outputs. It does not describe a generative text-bio foundational model.","The abstract describes a deep learning-based radiomic subtyping study using MAE for feature extraction and clustering, with no natural-language text component, no text-bio bridge, and no generative mechanism; it is an application wrapper and not eligible.",IMG-33. Unveiling glioblastoma heterogeneity with deep learning derived MRI subtyping: insights from the global ReSPOND consortium,"This study aims to identify distinct imaging subtypes of glioblastoma using multi-modal MRIs from the ReSPOND consortium, providing insights into tumor heterogeneity to inform personalized treatment approaches.
