 to distillate biological knowledge from text and deep learning methodologies capturing complex patterns in gene expression data, GRNPT overcomes the limitations of traditional GRN inference methods and enables more accurate and comprehensive understanding of gene regulatory dynamics.",exclude_uncertain_unstable,EXCLUDE,application_wrapper,,application_wrapper,no,no,no,yes,none,none,none,clear_exclude,The abstract describes a Transformer model that leverages LLM embeddings as side information for GRN inference without generating text or providing a multimodal text‑bio generation; thus it is an application‑wrapper paper and excluded.,"The work presents a novel Transformer framework that integrates LLM embeddings as side information for GRN inference, which is a downstream predictive task; embeddings alone do not constitute a substantive natural-language text component or bridge, so it is an application wrapper.","The abstract presents a novel Transformer framework for GRN inference without mentioning any decoder, autoregressive, or other generative mechanism (generative_model_present=no). It explicitly integrates large language model embeddings, indicating use of a foundation model (foundation_model_evidence=yes).",The abstract describes a Transformer model that leverages LLM embeddings as side information for GRN inference without generating text or providing a multimodal text‑bio generation; thus it is an application‑wrapper paper and excluded.
