./analysis/cross_agent_screening_agreement_current_3ds_2gpt/cross_model_decisions.csv:192:                Pre-trained language models promise to enrich analyses of single-cell data with additional layers of information leveraging large text corpora. Yet, it is still unclear how to achieve optimal alignment with the primary quantitative single-cell data. To address this, we construct text-based training datasets from both scRNA-seq data and biomedical literature targeted to the experimental setting at hand. We then jointly train language models on both information sources to learn a common, literature-enriched representation. Our examples on functionality, disease associations, and temporal trajectories show the potential of knowledge-augmented embeddings as a generalizable and interpretable strategy for enriching single-cell analysis pipelines.",include_decision_unstable,EXCLUDE,application_wrapper,,application_wrapper,yes,yes,no,no,text-based training datasets from both scRNA-seq data and biomedical literature,"learn a common, literature-enriched representation",none,wrapper_boundary,"The abstract describes joint training of pre-trained language models on scRNA-seq data and biomedical literature to produce enriched embeddings, not a generative model. This is an application wrapper using text to augment biological data, not a new multimodal generative foundation model.","The abstract presents a primary model that jointly trains language models on scRNA-seq data and biomedical literature to produce a common representation, clearly involving biological modality, text component, and a text-bio bridge.","The abstract describes using pre-trained language models to enrich scRNA-seq data representations via joint training, but does not propose a new generative model or describe a generative mechanism; it is an application wrapper around existing models.","The abstract describes joint training of pre-trained language models on scRNA-seq data and biomedical literature to produce enriched embeddings, not a generative model. This is an application wrapper using text to augment biological data, not a new multimodal generative foundation model.",Adding layers of information to scRNA-seq data using pre-trained language models,"Abstract
