e models and transfer learning, not a generative or foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"comprehensive review\"; \"predicting colorectal cancer metastases\"; \"predictive models\""},{"record_id":"rec_000144","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a perspective proposing multimodal integration for precision immunology, not a model paper. It mentions transparent multimodal AI as a future translation tool, but gives no evidence of a generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"In this perspective\"; \"outline technical and strategic steps\"; \"transparent multimodal AI\""}]}
