./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0224.stderr.log:1581:./data/screening_codex_2026-06-10/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0003.stderr.log:1718:./data/screening_codex_2026-06-10/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0033.stderr.log:2075:./data/screening_codex_2026-06-10/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0008.response.txt:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_000057","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract explicitly says this is a review of computational tools and paradigms. It does not describe a new generative model or foundation-model training.","evidence_snippet":"\"This review analyzes the field\" and \"we examine the evolution\" of computational tools."},{"record_id":"rec_000058","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a predictive deep learning model for recurrence risk, not a generative architecture. The abstract describes classification/prediction from histopathology and clinical variables.","evidence_snippet":"\"clinically interpretable multimodal prediction model\" that \"predict[s] postoperative recurrence\"."},{"record_id":"rec_000059","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The model is a multimodal diagnostic framework using feature enhancement and contrastive alignment for classification. No decoder, autoregressive, or other generative mechanism is described.","evidence_snippet":"\"multimodal diagnostic framework\" and \"breast cancer classification\"."},{"record_id":"rec_000060","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"ppIRIS is presented as a deep learning framework to predict PPIs from sequence, which is a discriminative prediction task. The abstract does not describe a generative model.","evidence_snippet":"\"predict PPIs directly from sequence\" and \"deep learning framework\"."},{"record_id":"rec_000061","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"ProteomeLM is a transformer-based language model trained on entire proteomes across diverse species, which supports foundation-model-like evidence. However, the abstract describes masked reconstruction rather than a clearly generative decoder or autoregressive model.","evidence_snippet":"\"trained to reconstruct masked protein embeddings\" and \"operates on entire proteomes from species spanning the tree of life\"."},{"record_id":"rec_000062","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract states this is a review of how genomic, environmental, and phenomic information can be integrated. It does not present a new generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"This review examines\" integration of genomic, environmental, and phenomic information."},{"record_id":"rec_000063","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The work centers on a prediction algorithm that integrates a pretrained protein-language model with gene weights for pathway-level inference. That is an application of an existing model, not evidence of a new generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"integrating a pretrained protein-language model and gene weights\" to \"establish a prediction algorithm\"."},{"record_id":"rec_000064","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a review of emerging multimodal models and AI foundation models in epilepsy, not a primary generative model paper. The abstract summarizes examples and challenges rather than introducing a model.","evidence_snippet":"\"In this review, we summarise\" and \"We describe AI foundation models\"."}]}
./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0224.stderr.log:1582:./data/screening_codex_2026-06-10/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0003.stderr.log:1719:./data/screening_codex_2026-06-10/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0033.stderr.log:2076:./data/screening_codex_2026-06-10/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0019.response.txt:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_000145","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"generative_status_unclear","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes a systematic evaluation of 11 genomic language models and critiques their pretraining paradigm, rather than presenting a new model. It does not clearly specify a generative architecture or broader foundation-model properties.","evidence_snippet":"“systematically evaluated 11 representative gLMs” and “canonical sequence-only self-supervised pretraining paradigm”"},{"record_id":"rec_000146","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Gemini Pro is used zero-shot as an existing LLM to make ranked primary-site predictions, so this is an application wrapper rather than a new model paper. The abstract explicitly identifies it as a large language model used without fine-tuning.","evidence_snippet":"“Large Language Models (LLMs), such as Gemini Pro” and “zero-shot prompt”"},{"record_id":"rec_000147","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"generative_status_unclear","decision_rationale":"This is a broad review of AI in drug discovery, not a primary generative model paper. It mentions generative models in passing, but the abstract does not describe a specific generative architecture or foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"“This review provides a comprehensive analysis” and “generative models such as GANs and reinforcement learning”"},{"record_id":"rec_000148","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract presents SciCore-Omics as a tri-modal foundation model trained on a large paired image-gene-text dataset. It also reports zero-shot generalization and language-grounded outputs, supporting both generative and foundation-model evidence.","evidence_snippet":"“the first tri-modal foundation model linking histology images, spatial transcriptomics, and biological language” and “robust zero-shot generalization”"},{"record_id":"rec_000149","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"generative_status_unclear","decision_rationale":"The abstract is a review of AI-driven ASD diagnosis across modalities and methods. It does not describe a new generative architecture or provide foundation-model evidence.","evidence_snippet":"“This review provides a comprehensive analysis” and “deep learning, traditional machine learning, and multimodal fusion techniques”"},{"record_id":"rec_000150","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"GRNPred is an encoder-based graph transformer with masked gene-expression reconstruction and supervised edge prediction, which is predictive rather than clearly generative. The abstract does describe self-supervised pretraining on unlabeled data, but not a foundation model with broad applicability.","evidence_snippet":"“graph transformer encoder” and “masked gene-expression reconstruction”"},{"record_id":"rec_000151","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes multimodal chemical-screening analysis frameworks for decoding perturbation effects, not a generative model. It is a methods paper about screening and inference, with no foundation-model evidence.","evidence_snippet":"“we develop MoCAVI, a contrastive analysis framework” and “PERCISTRA, a pipeline that infers causal links”"},{"record_id":"rec_000152","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"H2O is presented as a generalist foundation model trained on a very large pan-tissue paired dataset and used to infer spatial transcriptomics and proteomics from histology. The abstract explicitly emphasizes broad generalizability and computational generation of omics landscapes.","evidence_snippet":"“a foundation model bridging histopathology to spatial multi-omics profiling” and “trained on a pan-tissue dataset of 1.3 million paired H&E-spatial patches”"}]}
./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0224.stderr.log:1583:./data/screening_codex_2026-06-10/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0003.stderr.log:1720:./data/screening_codex_2026-06-10/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0033.stderr.log:2077:./data/screening_codex_2026-06-10/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0012.stdout.log:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_000089","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract explicitly says this is a review summarizing recent advances in WSI-based DL models. It discusses diagnostic/predictive pipelines rather than a generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"This review summarizes recent advances in WSI-based DL models\"; \"Typical pipelines include ... prediction\""},{"record_id":"rec_000090","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"triAMPh is a predictive framework built from a graph predictor, XGBoost, and an MLP using features from biological LLMs. The abstract does not describe a generative architecture or a foundation model of its own.","evidence_snippet":"\"integrates a heterogeneous graph attention network-based link predictor, Extreme Gradient Boosting, and a multilayer perceptron\"; \"trained on features from biological large language models\""},{"record_id":"rec_000091","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"generative_status_unclear","decision_rationale":"The abstract claims cross-modal translation using a single-cell foundation model, but it does not specify a clearly generative mechanism. It also does not provide enough detail on pretraining or broad applicability to confirm foundation-model characteristics.","evidence_snippet":"\"a single-cell foundation model can perform this translation via adversarial fine-tuning\""},{"record_id":"rec_000092","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"PlantGFM is explicitly described as a genomic foundation model with pretraining on 10.84 billion nucleotides. The abstract states that it supports sequence generation and de novo design.","evidence_snippet":"\"pre-trained on 10.84 billion nucleotides\"; \"supports long-context ... prediction and sequence generation\"; \"de novo design of novel candidates\""},{"record_id":"rec_000093","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"DamageFormer is presented as a multimodal detection/localization framework, and LesionBERT is a damage-aware genomic foundation model. The abstract does not show a genuinely generative architecture, despite transfer to unseen lesion types.","evidence_snippet":"\"damage-aware genomic foundation model built upon DNABERT-2\"; \"framework for detection and localization of DNA lesions\"; \"generalizes to chemically distinct guanine lesions\""},{"record_id":"rec_000094","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a single-cell transcriptome profiling and expression-atlas/resource paper, not a model paper. The abstract contains no generative architecture or foundation-model evidence.","evidence_snippet":"\"comprehensive single-cell transcriptome profiling\"; \"provides an enhanced type 2 diabetes expression-atlas\"; \"novel genomic resource\""},{"record_id":"rec_000095","paper_type":"unclear","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"paper_type_unclear","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes a spatial transcriptomics/scRNA-seq biology study and validation of cell states, not a generative model. It does not provide foundation-model evidence.","evidence_snippet":"\"We describe the use of true single-cell resolution spatial transcriptomics\"; \"identify and localize key transcriptional programs in situ\""},{"record_id":"rec_000096","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"SI-SimCLR is a self-supervised representation-learning framework for reconstructing phenotypic landscapes, but the abstract does not describe a generative model. It also lacks evidence of foundation-model-style pretraining or broad transfer.","evidence_snippet":"\"self-supervised learning framework\"; \"learns biologically informative representations\"; \"enables reconstruction of cellular phenotypic landscapes\""}]}
