./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0224.stderr.log:1607:./data/screening_codex_2026-06-10/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0003.stderr.log:1841:./data/screening_codex_2026-06-10/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0033.stderr.log:2220:./data/screening_codex_2026-06-10/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0025.stdout.log:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_000193","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a review of bioactive peptide discovery and translation, not a primary model paper. It mentions generative design only as a field-level approach, not as a described architecture.","evidence_snippet":"\"from computational discovery and data bottlenecks to precision medicine translation\"; discusses \"machine learning classifiers and protein language models to ... generative design\""},{"record_id":"rec_000194","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Bio-BLIP is presented as a pretrained multimodal architecture using an LLM backbone with zero-shot downstream use. The abstract explicitly emphasizes transfer and generalization without task-specific fine-tuning.","evidence_snippet":"\"multimodal Q-former based architecture\"; \"pretrained\"; \"generalize to complex reasoning tasks without task-specific fine-tuning\"; \"zero-shot\""},{"record_id":"rec_000195","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The study evaluates models for predicting stress-induced gene expression, which is a predictive task rather than a generative one. It does mention a transformer-based genomic language model pre-trained on plant genomes, which is foundation-model-like evidence.","evidence_snippet":"\"CNN and a transformer-based genomic language model pre-trained on plant genomes to predict changes in gene expression\""},{"record_id":"rec_000196","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is an application of DNABERT embeddings for DNA sequence alignment, not a new generative model. The abstract frames DNABERT as the existing large language model component in a downstream workflow.","evidence_snippet":"\"combining deep learning with DNABERT embeddings\"; \"large transformer-based language model\"; \"DNA sequence alignment\""},{"record_id":"rec_000197","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"foundation_model_evidence_unclear","decision_rationale":"SYMOL is described as a self-supervised multimodal representation-learning framework for spatial transcriptomics integration, not a generative architecture. The abstract does not clearly establish that SYMOL itself has foundation-model-like pretraining or broad transferable scope.","evidence_snippet":"\"unified synergistic self-supervised multimodal framework\"; \"integrates spatial coordinates, gene expression, and histological images\"; uses \"pretrained large vision models\""},{"record_id":"rec_000198","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a review of AI in early cancer detection rather than a primary model paper. It summarizes CNNs and transformer-based models but does not present a candidate generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"This review summarizes recent progress and clinical applications of AI\"; \"including Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) and Transformer-based models\""},{"record_id":"rec_000199","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes a benchmarking guideline and new evaluation tasks for spatial transcriptomics foundation models. It is a benchmark/resource paper, not a generative model paper.","evidence_snippet":"\"A practical guideline for benchmarking unimodal and multimodal foundation models\"; \"introduce a new set of tasks and metrics\""},{"record_id":"rec_000200","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a multimodal survival prediction system that outputs risk scores and survival times, so it is predictive rather than generative. The abstract describes modality encoders and fusion, not a foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"multimodal deep learning framework for patient-level survival prediction\"; \"outputs continuous risk scores\"; \"feedforward encoders\""}]}
./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0224.stderr.log:1608:./data/screening_codex_2026-06-10/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0003.stderr.log:1842:./data/screening_codex_2026-06-10/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0033.stderr.log:2221:./data/screening_codex_2026-06-10/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0003.stdout.log:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_000017","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a narrative review, not an original model paper. It discusses ML/AI integrations and prior studies, but does not describe a generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"This narrative review synthesizes recent advances\"; mentions \"machine learning and artificial intelligence integrations\" and \"BioMapAI\"."},{"record_id":"rec_000018","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a review of pathology foundation models rather than a candidate model itself. It does provide clear foundation-model evidence in the form of broad generalization, self-supervised pretraining, and few-shot adaptability.","evidence_snippet":"\"pathology foundation models\"; \"massive whole-slide image repositories and self-supervised Vision Transformer architectures\"; \"broad generalization and few-shot adaptability\"."},{"record_id":"rec_000019","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes a prognostic classification pipeline and risk model, not a generative architecture. No foundation-model-like pretraining or transferable model evidence is given.","evidence_snippet":"\"classification using machine learning algorithms\"; \"construct a risk model\"; \"stratified risk groups\"."},{"record_id":"rec_000020","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"generative_status_unclear","decision_rationale":"The work is a graph contrastive autoencoder for spatial transcriptomics, but the abstract emphasizes representation learning and batch correction rather than an explicitly generative mechanism. It does not show foundation-model-like pretraining or broad transferable applicability.","evidence_snippet":"\"graph contrastive autoencoder framework\"; \"self-supervised strategy\"; \"batch-effect correction without manual intervention\"."},{"record_id":"rec_000021","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"generative_status_unclear","decision_rationale":"This is a fine-tuned predictor for missense interpretation, so the abstract does not clearly establish a genuinely generative architecture. It does show foundation-model-like evidence through multi-species pretraining, backbone transfer, and zero-shot use of the pretrained model.","evidence_snippet":"\"genomic language models\"; \"multi-species pretraining provided the strongest backbone-level advantage\"; \"zero-shot scoring from the same pretrained model\"."},{"record_id":"rec_000022","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a review that surveys deep learning and generative design for orthopaedic protein degradation. It does not present a candidate generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"In this review\"; \"examine how emerging DL architectures... and generative design\"."},{"record_id":"rec_000023","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes cross-TF prediction and transfer learning for binding-site prediction, which is a predictive task rather than a generative model. It does not provide evidence of foundation-model-style broad pretraining or transferable representations beyond the task setup.","evidence_snippet":"\"predict in vivo TF binding sites\"; \"cross-TF transfer learning scheme\"; \"DNA language model embeddings increase model performance\"."},{"record_id":"rec_000024","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The framework wraps established LLM and protein-embedding models for pathogenicity prediction rather than introducing a new generative model. The abstract is centered on embedding-based classification and nearest-neighbor prediction.","evidence_snippet":"\"uses... Large Language Models (LLMs)\"; \"pathogenicity... predicted by its proximity\"; \"framework, VUS.Life\"."}]}
