:"rec_000047","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"scLLMDA uses a pretrained DNA language model as an embedding source for cell type annotation, which is an applied downstream system rather than a generative model. The abstract does not describe broad pretraining or other foundation-model evidence for the candidate method itself.","evidence_snippet":"\"uses a pretrained DNA-specific language model to generate contextual embeddings\" and \"cell type annotation\""},{"record_id":"rec_000048","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"M-GNN is a multi-modal graph neural network for cancer driver gene prediction, which is predictive rather than generative. The mention of a pre-trained teacher model is distillation support, not evidence of a foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"A multi-modal GNN framework for cancer driver gene prediction\" and \"using soft labels from a pre-trained teacher model\""}]}
