nly during training\""},{"record_id":"rec_000103","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The title and abstract indicate a review of current and future AI applications in surgery, not an original model paper. No generative or foundation-model evidence is presented.","evidence_snippet":"\"This review evaluates and critically analyzes current... applications of AI in surgery\""},{"record_id":"rec_000104","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"SpaRank is a transferable deconvolution framework, but the abstract frames it as inference on ranked feature sequences rather than a generative model. It does provide evidence of foundation-model-like transfer through pretrain-transfer behavior and cross-context generalization.","evidence_snippet":"\"adapting the rank-based encodings of single-cell foundation models\" and \"enabling a pretrain-transfer paradigm\""}]}
