":"Only the title and author list are present; no abstract methods or results are provided."},{"record_id":"rec_000188","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"GMRNet is a classification model using ResNet50 feature extraction and fusion, not a generative system. The abstract does not indicate broad pretraining or foundation-model-like transferability.","evidence_snippet":"“deep learning model for glioma subtype classification” and “uses a ResNet50 backbone to extract multiscale features”"},{"record_id":"rec_000189","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a multimodal classification pipeline based on cross-modal self-attention, not a generative model. The abstract provides no evidence of foundation-model-style pretraining or broad applicability.","evidence_snippet":"“proposes a cross-modal transformer-based approach” for “breast cancer subtype classification”"},{"record_id":"rec_000190","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes an explainable deep learning forecasting model for Huntington’s disease, which is predictive rather than generative. It does not present foundation-model evidence such as broad pretraining or transferable representations.","evidence_snippet":"“proposed for genetic prediction of Huntington’s disease” and “improved predictive performance compared to conventional approaches”"},{"record_id":"rec_000191","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract explicitly describes a sequence-to-sequence Specificity Foundation Model and reports the same architecture used across six domains. That is evidence of both a generative-style architecture and foundation-model-like broad transfer.","evidence_snippet":"“a single neural network architecture for cross-modal binding prediction” and “six SFMs across six molecular recognition domains ... using the identical architecture without modification”"},{"record_id":"rec_000192","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a review that maps AI methods onto ADC development rather than proposing a new model. The abstract discusses generative AI as a topic, but not a candidate generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"“this review provides a systematic and comprehensive conceptual framework” and “generative AI for neuromodulatory payload design”"}]}
