./data/screening_codex_full_2026-07-06/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0224.stderr.log:1657:./data/screening_codex_2026-06-10/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0003.stderr.log:2163:./data/screening_codex_2026-06-10/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0033.stderr.log:2605:./data/screening_codex_2026-06-10/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0014.stdout.log:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"rec_000105","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract explicitly says this is a “thorough analysis” and “comprehensive review” of deep learning methods. It discusses segmentation and prediction methods, not a new generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"“This is a thorough analysis ... a comprehensive review”"},{"record_id":"rec_000106","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract is a broad overview of AI in tumor evolution and precision oncology, without describing a specific model architecture. It reads as a narrative review rather than a primary generative model paper.","evidence_snippet":"“AI tools have the ability to integrate and analyze large-scale multi-omics, imaging and clinical data”"},{"record_id":"rec_000107","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"generative_status_unclear","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes a self-supervised foundation model trained on thousands of tumors and used on unseen H&E images across multiple cancer types. It does not explicitly state a generative mechanism such as a decoder, autoregressive model, or diffusion model.","evidence_snippet":"“A self-supervised AI foundation model was trained ... using purpose-built multimodal training data from thousands of human tumors”"},{"record_id":"rec_000108","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a scoping review of 20 studies, not a primary model report. The mentions of LLM and foundation models are survey content rather than evidence for a candidate generative model.","evidence_snippet":"“This scoping review systematically maps AI- and DL-based methodologies”"},{"record_id":"rec_000109","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC4_no_foundation_model_evidence","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract explicitly describes a “conditional variational autoencoder framework,” which is a genuinely generative architecture. It presents a task-specific virtual cell model, but not clear foundation-model-like broad pretraining or applicability.","evidence_snippet":"“a lightweight conditional variational autoencoder framework”"},{"record_id":"rec_000110","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The model is described as a “modernized BERT-style back-bone,” which is encoder-style rather than clearly generative. The abstract does give foundation-model evidence through genomic sequence modeling and benchmark performance.","evidence_snippet":"“modernized BERT-style back-bone ... adapted to genomic sequence modeling”"},{"record_id":"rec_000111","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract states that the authors performed a “systematic review” of AI-based prognostic models. It summarizes existing recurrence and RFS prediction studies rather than describing a new generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"“We performed a contemporary systematic review”"},{"record_id":"rec_000112","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract applies pre-trained immune system models and a peripheral immune system encoder to predict response and toxicity. This is an application of existing foundation-like models, not a new generative model.","evidence_snippet":"“pre-trained immunotype models” and “a peripheral immune system encoder trained on the BostonGene patient database”"}]}
