e architecture is described. The abstract does not provide foundation-model evidence.","evidence_snippet":"\"an ai-based system of targeted drug delivery\"; \"machine learning, deep learning and reinforcement learning in a single system\""},{"record_id":"rec_000084","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The paper is a diagnostic/methodological study about existing genomic foundation models, not a generative model itself. It does, however, explicitly involve broad foundation models with zero-shot use and cross-architecture analysis.","evidence_snippet":"\"Across three architecturally distinct foundation models\"; \"sequence foundation models offer a zero-shot route\""},{"record_id":"rec_000085","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a systematic review of explainable AI in malaria prediction. The abstract discusses ensemble and deep-learning classifiers, not a generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"This systematic review synthesises\"; \"ensemble learning models, particularly Random Forest and XGBoost\""},{"record_id":"rec_000086","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a narrative review of machine learning methods and applications in healthcare. It mentions foundation models as a topic, but does not present a new generative model or model evidence.","evidence_snippet":"\"This narrative review explains the principles of machine learning\"; \"Evidence ... is discussed alongside ... foundation models\""},{"record_id":"rec_000087","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract presents an end-to-end platform that combines a pretrained patient representation model with an LLM-driven workflow, which reads as an application layer rather than a new generative model. It does provide foundation-model evidence through large-scale pretraining on millions of cells and patients.","evidence_snippet":"\"a patient representation model trained on over 20 million cells across 4,479 patients\"; \"a large language model-driven workflow\""},{"record_id":"rec_000088","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Haiku is a new tri-modal contrastive learning model, but the abstract does not describe a genuinely generative architecture. Its large-scale training and zero-shot biomarker inference support foundation-model-like characteristics.","evidence_snippet":"\"a tri-modal contrastive learning model trained on multiplexed immunofluorescence\"; \"supports zero-shot biomarker inference\""}]}
