e":"no"}}},{"record_id":"rec_000274","title":"A foundation model of cancer genotype enables precise predictions of therapeutic response","abstract":"Abstract\n                  While genetic sequencing is routine in cancer care, translating a tumor’s complex mutation profile into actionable treatment decisions remains a central challenge. MutationProjector is pre-trained from a large corpus of genomic alterations across 30,000+ tumors, integrated with extensive molecular knowledge. The resulting projection reveals a tumor’s altered molecular pathways, facilitating model interpretation, and it accurately reconstructs held-out mutations, demonstrating model generalization. When applied to predict immunotherapy or chemotherapy resistance across multiple cancer types and cohorts, MutationProjector achieves or exceeds state-of-the-art performance in all contexts. It identifies unexpected biomarkers, including KMT2D mutation in immunotherapy sensitivity and joint alteration of SMARCA4 and STK11 in immunotherapy resistance. These results establish a unifying framework for connecting tumor genotypes to biological mechanisms and therapeutic outcomes.","doi":"10.1158/2159-8290.cd-25-1735","year":"2026","venue":"Cancer …","sources":["google_scholar"],"first_pass_outputs":{"scope_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_000274","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes a pretrained cancer-genotype foundation model built from genomic alterations and molecular knowledge. No substantive text/language component is described.","evidence_snippet":"“pre-trained from a large corpus of genomic alterations across 30,000+ tumors”"},"architecture_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_000274","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"generative_status_unclear","decision_rationale":"The abstract clearly describes a pre-trained model on 30,000+ tumors with generalization across cancer types, which is foundation-model-like evidence. It does not explicitly state a decoder, autoregressive, or other clearly generative mechanism, so generative status is unclear.","evidence_snippet":"\"pre-trained from a large corpus of genomic alterations across 30,000+ tumors\" and \"accurately reconstructs held-out mutations\""},"python_gate":{"provisional_decision":"ADJUDICATE","provisional_code":"EC2_no_text_component","adjudication_reason":"criterion_unclear_or_reviewer_conflict","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"yes"}}},{"record_id":"rec_000276","title":"Statistical and Artificial Intelligence Methods for Analyzing Single-Cell and Genomic Data","abstract":"2.4 Pseudotime and marker gene expression on the mouse haematopoietic stem and  All  the plots in (ae) and (hk) are scatterplots of the two dimensional single-cell data given by UMAP","doi":"","year":"2026","venue":"NA","sources":["google_scholar"],"first_pass_outputs":{"scope_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_000276","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This reads as a methods overview on statistical and AI approaches for single-cell and genomic data. The abstract snippet does not describe a primary text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"“Statistical and Artificial Intelligence Methods for Analyzing Single-Cell and Genomic Data”"},"architecture_reviewer":{"record_id":"rec_000276","paper_type":"review_editorial","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":